The IT Security Office is aware of a phishing campaign targeting Virginia Tec=
h employees and graduate assistants.

The messages:
- have the subject "Payroll Adjustment - Action Required" or "Updated Direct =
Deposit Form"
- claim to come from "VT HR Payroll" but are sent from external addresses
- link to a fake VT login page that asks for your PID, password and a Duo code

What to do:
- Do not click the link or enter your credentials.
- Use the "Report Phishing" button in Outlook, or forward the message as an a=
ttachment to abuse@vt.edu.
- If you already entered your password, change it at https://onecampus.vt.edu=
 and contact 4Help at 540-231-4357.

VT HR will never ask you to update direct deposit information through an emai=
led link.

